+## Safeguarding and Protected-Participant Terms Added in V1.2
+
+### Minor
+
+Definition: A person treated as under the age of legal majority or otherwise subject to minor-specific protection under applicable law or the governing participation context. EquineSync shall use a default under-18 presumption unless reliable jurisdictional evidence establishes a different rule.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Protected Participant; Guardian; Age of Majority
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Protected Participant
+
+Definition: A person entitled to heightened participation, privacy, communication, access, or safeguarding protections because the person is: - a minor; - subject to guardianship, conservatorship, supported decision-making, or comparable authority arrangement; - materially limited in the ability to provide informed authorization for the relevant matter; - subject to an active safeguarding or protective restriction; - an alleged victim, reporter, or witness whose identity or safety requires additional protection; - temporarily designated through a documented protective process. Protected-participant status must not be inferred solely from diagnosis, disability, age, communication style, reputation, or administrative convenience.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Minor; Guardian; Protective Restriction
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Guardian
+
+Definition: A person or legally recognized entity holding verified and scoped authority or responsibility for a minor or protected participant. Guardian status is distinct from parentage, household relationship, payer status, emergency-contact status, account ownership, and general caregiving.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Guardian Authority Record; Minor; Protected Participant
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Guardian Authority Record
+
+Definition: The governed record identifying the guardian, protected participant, authority source, scope, restrictions, effective dates, evidence, notice rights, communication rights, pickup rights, and dispute status.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Guardian; Authority Basis; Effective Time
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Assent
+
+Definition: An age-appropriate and capacity-appropriate expression of agreement, willingness, or participation by a minor or protected participant. Assent is distinct from legal consent, guardian authorization, contractual assent, and permission.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Consent; Protected Refusal; Guardian Authorization
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Protected Refusal
+
+Definition: A clear expression by a minor or protected participant declining optional publicity, optional communication, optional research, nonessential social exposure, or another non-mandatory activity. A protected refusal must be respected unless a documented safety, legal, emergency, or essential-care basis requires a different action.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Assent; Optional Participation; Withdrawal
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Adult Third Party
+
+Definition: An adult other than the protected participant's verified parent or guardian who interacts with the protected participant through a coaching, training, instructional, employment, volunteer, provider, facility, transportation, service, community, or operational role.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Trainer or Coach; Adult Eligibility State; Guardian
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Trainer or Coach
+
+Definition: An adult or organization providing riding, horse-care, athletic, instructional, training, performance, or related guidance, regardless of title, compensation, employment status, or platform role.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Adult Third Party; Adult Eligibility State; Protected Participant
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Safeguarding Concern
+
+Definition: Information indicating possible abuse, neglect, exploitation, grooming, harassment, boundary violation, retaliation, prohibited communication, unsafe release, unsafe transportation, coercion, privacy violation, or another threat to a protected participant.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Protected Safeguarding Intake; Safeguarding Case; Protective Restriction
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Safeguarding Authority
+
+Definition: A qualified and expressly authorized person or body permitted to receive, triage, preserve, restrict, review, escalate, or resolve safeguarding matters within a defined scope.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Safeguarding Case; Protective Restriction; External Reporting Duty
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Protective Restriction
+
+Definition: A temporary or continuing limitation on contact, messaging, access, assignment, pickup, transportation, media, visibility, participation, or another capability imposed to reduce safeguarding risk. A protective restriction is not itself a finding of guilt or liability.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Safety Plan; Emergency Access; Safeguarding Case
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Ordinary Electronic Communication
+
+Definition: Any non-safeguarding message, reply, file transmission, media transmission, email, SMS, integrated notice response, chat, or comparable electronic exchange between an adult third party and a minor.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Communication Consent; Protected Safeguarding Intake; Guardian
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Protected Safeguarding Intake
+
+Definition: A dedicated channel for reporting safeguarding concerns that is segregated from ordinary communication, subject to restricted visibility, and capable of protecting a reporter from unsafe guardian or accused-person disclosure.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Safeguarding Concern; Confidential Report; Guardian Notification Exception
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Adult Eligibility State
+
+Definition: The governed status determining whether an adult may receive protected-participant access, assignments, communication capability, pickup authority, transportation authority, or another protected role.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Adult Third Party; Trainer or Coach; Protective Restriction
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Observable and Interruptible Interaction
+
+Definition: An interaction structured so that an authorized person can observe, enter, interrupt, or review the interaction without hidden or isolated conditions inconsistent with the approved activity.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Protected Participant; Supervision; Safety Plan
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Safeguarding Case
+
+Definition: The governed case object that connects an intake, affected participants, reporter and witness information, alleged conduct, responding persons, interim protections, evidence, external referrals, review actions, decisions, appeals, and closure history. A Safeguarding Case is distinct from an ordinary incident, message thread, personnel note, customer-support ticket, or generic task.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Safeguarding Concern; Responding Person; Audit Evidence
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Responding Person
+
+Definition: A person whose conduct, access, eligibility, communication, or relationship is being reviewed in connection with a safeguarding concern. A Responding Person must not be labeled as an offender, abuser, dangerous person, or responsible party merely because a report or interim restriction exists.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Safeguarding Case; Procedural Fairness; Protective Restriction
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Good-Faith Report
+
+Definition: A report made with an honest belief that the information may indicate a safeguarding concern, even if the concern is later unsubstantiated, mistaken, incomplete, or unable to be determined.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Safeguarding Concern; Non-Retaliation; Knowingly False or Malicious Report
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Knowingly False or Malicious Report
+
+Definition: A report shown through an authorized process to have been intentionally fabricated or knowingly submitted for an improper retaliatory or harmful purpose. A mistaken, unsupported, withdrawn, or unsubstantiated report is not, without additional evidence, a knowingly false or malicious report.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Good-Faith Report; Retaliation; Safeguarding Case
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### External Reporting Duty
+
+Definition: A legal, regulatory, governing-body, insurance, contractual, emergency, or professional duty requiring information or a concern to be reported outside EquineSync or outside the customer organization. An internal workflow must not delay, replace, narrow, or falsely represent satisfaction of an External Reporting Duty.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Mandated Reporter; Safeguarding Authority; Notice
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Mandated Reporter
+
+Definition: A person or role that may have a legally or professionally imposed duty to report specified concerns to an external authority. EquineSync may record and support the workflow but does not independently determine whether a person is a Mandated Reporter or provide legal advice.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: External Reporting Duty; Safeguarding Concern; Safeguarding Authority
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Safety Plan
+
+Definition: A documented, minimum-necessary set of temporary or continuing measures designed to reduce identified risk while preserving participation, privacy, fairness, and review rights to the extent reasonably possible.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Protective Restriction; Protected Participant; Emergency Action
+
+Status: Canonical
+
+### Conflict of Interest
+
+Definition: A personal, supervisory, financial, familial, organizational, legal, or other interest that could materially impair, or reasonably appear to impair, a person's impartial handling of a safeguarding matter.
+
+Primary Owner: MASTER_MINOR_GUARDIANSHIP_SAFEGUARDING_AND_PROTECTED_PARTICIPANT_MODEL_V1_1
+
+Related Terms: Recusal; Safeguarding Authority; Independent Review
+
+Status: Canonical
+
